"releaseNotes":"New in version 4.2:\n- Does your loved one's home care take part? Then the home care organisation can invite you. CareWall then shows who is coming and when and what the care team shares, and you can message or call the team.\n- Care agreements: when the home care asks you to sign an agreement, you see it on your start screen. Read it, fill in what is needed and sign with your finger. Signed agreements stay under Care Agreements.\n- Chat with the care team: reply, edit, delete and react.\n- For carers: photos, files, voice messages, forwarding and search in the team chat; for a client with several care plans you choose the right plan for your report; the knowledge base with folders; PDFs and certificates open properly; finishing a lesson goes on to the next one.\n- Your profile shows the right language, prices and measurements are in your own language, and many small improvements.", "version":"4.2.0", "wrapperType":"software", "currency":"USD", 
"description":"Caring for someone you love, together with your family? With CareWall everyone knows what is going on and who does what, without endless messages and loose lists.\n\nONE CARE CIRCLE, EVERYONE IN THE LOOP\nCreate a care circle for your mother, father, grandma or grandpa and invite the family. Everyone sees the same: what happens today, what still needs doing and how things are going.\n\nWHO DOES WHAT? EVERYONE KNOWS\n• A shared schedule: add moments and let family members say who goes.\n• A calendar with appointments at the GP, the hospital or the hairdresser.\n• Tick off tasks and medication together, so nobody does anything twice or forgets.\n\nNEED A HAND? ASK YOUR FAMILY\nAsk for help with shopping, transport or a visit. Whoever can takes it on, and everyone sees it.\n\nSTAY CLOSE, EVEN FROM FAR AWAY\nShare an update or a photo in the care feed, react to each other and chat with the whole care circle or one person.\n\nALL CARE DETAILS IN ONE PLACE\nThe care file with contacts, appointments, medical details and documents. Plus short courses (in Dutch) about caring for a loved one and an assistant that thinks along.\n\nSAFE AND PRIVATE\nOnly the people you invite see your care circle.\n\nFREE TO START\nStart free with one care circle and two members. More family members or more care circles? Choose Family Pro: unlimited, with a 14-day free trial first.\n\nFOR CARE PROFESSIONALS\nDoes your home care organisation use Nedap Ons? Then care professionals can use CareWall too, for their route, clients and reports.\n\nCareWall is available in Dutch, English and Arabic.", "averageUserRatingForCurrentVersion":0, "averageUserRating":0, "trackCensoredName":"CareWall: caregiving & family", "languageCodesISO2A":["EN"], "fileSizeBytes":"58953728", "formattedPrice":"Free", "contentAdvisoryRating":"4+", "userRatingCountForCurrentVersion":0, "trackViewUrl":"https://apps.apple.com/us/app/carewall-caregiving-family/id6502579279?uo=4", "trackContentRating":"4+", "trackI